  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Phase 1**\n\nI\'m now diving into Phase 1 of planning-mode! I\'m prepping to ask a few targeted multiple-choice questions using the `ask_question` tool. The goal is to keep things clean and concise in my query formulation. I\'ll aim for 2\342\200\2234 questions total, as per the established guidelines for this phase.\n\n\n**Refining User Queries**\n\nI\'m now revising my query design for Phase 1, focusing on concise, plain-text labels for multiple-choice options, keeping them under ten words. I\'ll flag the best choices with \"(Recommended)\". I will yield immediately after the `ask_question` tool is called. No `implementation_plan.md` in Turn 1, and no outputting the plan in chat. I am now focusing on genuine user preferences and ambiguities to make the questions genuinely helpful.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Product Options**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on product choices. I\'ve designed multiple-choice questions focusing on the user\'s preferred 3D visualization metaphor and visual aesthetic. I\'ve presented options such as a \"Floating Island Roadmap,\" \"Orbital Constellation,\" and \"Kinetic Workshop Assembly.\" My goal is to use this information to determine the final product vision.\n\n\n**Defining Initial Product State**\n\nI\'m now formulating questions about the initial user experience. I\'ve designed several multiple-choice questions focused on the default view, sync frequency, and notification behavior. I\'m prioritizing options that offer instant gratification and clear guidance for the user, such as a pre-loaded, popular repo, and real-time auto-syncing with in-app alerts.\n\n\n"
