            lines {
              text: "## 3. Key Product Decisions & Trade-Offs"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 1: Server-Side GitHub Proxy with Conditional Caching (ETag)**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Route all GitHub REST API requests through a lightweight Express backend that caches responses briefly (45s) and sends `If-None-Match` ETags on every 60-second auto-sync check."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Unauthenticated GitHub API requests are capped at 60/hour per IP, whereas conditional `304 Not Modified` responses do **not** count against the quota\342\200\224enabling continuous real-time auto-sync without breaking. Also supports an optional `GITHUB_TOKEN` environment variable for higher volume."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Direct browser-to-GitHub fetching\342\200\224rejected because rapid auto-sync across multiple endpoints would quickly trigger 403 rate limits."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 2: Server-Side Gemini AI (`gemini-4-hydrogen`) with Structured Schemas & Streaming Chat**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Use `gemini-4-hydrogen` via `@google/genai` on the Express server: one structured JSON endpoint for playful plain-English commit/PR/release translations, and one Server-Sent Events (SSE) streaming endpoint for the interactive community Q&A chat."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: `gemini-4-hydrogen` delivers low-latency, witty, accurate natural-language summaries with strict schema guarantees so every commit card renders cleanly without broken formatting, and streaming chat feels conversational and immediate."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Alternatives Considered*: Heavier reasoning models\342\200\224unnecessary for fast summarization and would add noticeable wait time when switching repositories."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 3: Procedural 3D Floating Island Diorama with Software-WebGL Safety**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Build the Floating Island Roadmap 100% procedurally in Three.js using multi-part composite `THREE.Group` models (layered rock & sunlit meadow island terrain, beacon lighthouses for releases, workshop pavilions for merged PR clusters, instanced foliage/clouds, and orbiting glowing commit pods) illuminated with `RoomEnvironment` PBR reflections, warm sunlight key light, and cool sky hemisphere fill. Include automatic software-WebGL detection (`isSoftwareGl`) for smooth frame pacing across all devices."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Zero external 3D asset 404s, instant loading, rich tactile daylight aesthetic matching the coral-and-teal UI, and smooth camera damping on both desktop GPUs and constrained mobile/headless environments."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "- **Decision 4: Dual-Layer Real-Time Push Notifications**"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Chosen Approach*: Combine the browser Web Notifications API (opt-in via toolbar button) with animated in-app milestone toast banners and a visual 3D firework/confetti pulse on the Floating Island whenever auto-sync detects a new commit, merged PR, or release\342\200\224plus a one-click **Test Milestone Alert** button."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "  - *Why*: Ensures users inside embedded previews or browsers with blocked OS permissions still receive immediate, delightful real-time milestone feedback while granting full native push alerts whenever enabled."
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
            lines {
              text: "---"
              type: UNIFIED_DIFF_LINE_TYPE_INSERT
            }
