  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Planning Frontend Architecture**\n\nI\'m laying out the core modules for the frontend. Specifically, I\'m starting with `src/utils/format.ts`, planning two critical utility functions: `formatCompactNumber`, to display numbers in a user-friendly way, and `formatRelativeTime`, to present time differences intuitively. This is the foundation for cleaner and easier-to-read data.\n\n\n**Refining Data Utilities**\n\nI\'ve expanded on the utility functions; focusing now on input normalization for repos. I\'m building `normalizeRepoInput` for client-side validation, ensuring a user-friendly preview. I\'m also curating a list of starter open-source repos, complete with descriptions and emojis. The goal is easy launcher cards. This will involve working on `src/utils/format.ts`.\n\n\n**Composing Lighting and Geometry**\n\nI\'m now integrating the lighting with the floating island models. I\'m focusing on a warm directional light with a tight shadow, balanced by a cool hemisphere light. The model composes into a layered floating island base, with sculpted cliff layers, a meadow plateau, and a winding pathway. The release milestone stations are envisioned as multi-part light houses. They\'ll have a stone foundation, a coral and cream tower, a metallic observation gallery, a glowing lantern dome, and a copper roof. These will be grouped and placed to represent real milestones.\n\n\n**Designing Island Milestones**\n\nI\'m now detailing the visual representation of GitHub activity within the 3D scene. I\'m visualizing merged pull requests as workshop pavilions, featuring a deck platform, timber pillars, and a teal roof. Contribution is visualized as a town square compass monument, scaled by top contributors. Recent commits are represented by orbiting energy pods, and I\'m adding instanced trees, rocks, and stylized clouds for detail.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'ve added celebratory confetti particles launching from each lighthouse. I\'m also building raycasting interactions for station inspection: hover highlights, smooth camera glides on click, and clean, non-obtrusive inspector cards with an \"Ask AI\" button. I\'m focusing on a collapsible bottom dock for camera presets, an auto-orbit toggle, and the celebration trigger, keeping the 3D island view uncluttered. I\'m also ensuring a WebGL context lost/restored guard.\n\n\n**Building Activity Charts**\n\nI\'m now building dynamic charts and leaderboards. I\'m focusing on `<VelocityAndContributors.tsx>`, implementing an animated Recharts area chart to visualize commit and merged PR cadence, using coral and teal gradients and a custom tooltip. I\'m also adding milestone progress bars and a top contributors spotlight with avatars and playful rank emoji medals. I\'m also creating `<ActivityFeed.tsx>`, which will have a latest release spotlight banner, interactive filter tabs, and jargon-free summaries.\n\n\n**Integrating AI Assistance**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI-powered features for deeper insights. I\'m developing an \"Explain with AI\" button that pre-populates the chat drawer with technical details for instant clarification. Within the chat drawer, I\'m building friendly starter prompts and real-time SSE consumption with markdown formatting and error handling. I\'m also adding in-app milestone toasts, incorporating animations for real-time progress updates.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "UsUCa8GAJdDN8L0P5dv1yQs"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_5636847193100746805"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export interface CuratedRepo {\\n  fullName: string;\\n  tagline: string;\\n  category: string;\\n  emoji: string;\\n  accent: \'coral\' | \'teal\' | \'marigold\' | \'indigo\';\\n}\\n\\nexport const CURATED_REPOS: CuratedRepo[] = [\\n  {\\n    fullName: \'facebook/react\',\\n    tagline: \'The UI library powering millions of modern web apps.\',\\n    category: \'Web Interfaces\',\\n    emoji: \'\342\232\233\357\270\217\',\\n    accent: \'teal\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    fullName: \'vercel/next.js\',\\n    tagline: \'Full-stack React framework built for fast, lively websites.\',\\n    category: \'App Framework\',\\n    emoji: \'\360\237\232\200\',\\n    accent: \'coral\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    fullName: \'vitejs/vite\',\\n    tagline: \'Lightning-fast toolkit that makes building web apps feel instant.\',\\n    category: \'Build Engine\',\\n    emoji: \'\342\232\241\',\\n    accent: \'marigold\',\\n  },\\n  {\\n    fullName: \'mrdoob/three.js\',\\n    tagline: \'Creative 3D graphics library bringing worlds to life in your browser.\',\\n    category: \'3D Graphics\',\\n    emoji: \'\360\237\217\235\357\270\217\',\\n    accent: \'teal\',\\n  },\\n];\\n\\nexport function normalizeRepoInput(raw: string): string | null {\\n  const cleaned = raw.trim().replace(/^@/, \'\');\\n  if (!cleaned) return null;\\n\\n  const urlMatch = cleaned.match(\\n    /^(?:https?:\\\\/\\\\/)?(?:www\\\\.)?github\\\\.com\\\\/([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)\\\\/([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)(?:\\\\/.*)?$/i\\n  );\\n  if (urlMatch) {\\n    return `${urlMatch[1]}/${urlMatch[2].replace(/\\\\.git$/i, \'\')}`;\\n  }\\n\\n  const shortMatch = cleaned.match(/^([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)\\\\/([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+)$/);\\n  if (shortMatch) {\\n    return `${shortMatch[1]}/${shortMatch[2].replace(/\\\\.git$/i, \'\')}`;\\n  }\\n\\n  return null;\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatCompactNumber(num: number): string {\\n  if (!Number.isFinite(num)) return \'0\';\\n  if (num >= 1_000_000) return `${(num / 1_000_000).toFixed(1)}M`;\\n  if (num >= 10_000) return `${Math.round(num / 1_000)}k`;\\n  if (num >= 1_000) return `${(num / 1_000).toFixed(1)}k`;\\n  return num.toLocaleString();\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatRelativeTime(isoDate: string): string {\\n  if (!isoDate) return \'recently\';\\n  const then = new Date(isoDate).getTime();\\n  if (Number.isNaN(then)) return \'recently\';\\n  const diffSec = Math.max(0, Math.floor((Date.now() - then) / 1000));\\n\\n  if (diffSec < 45) return \'just now\';\\n  const diffMin = Math.floor(diffSec / 60);\\n  if (diffMin < 60) return `${diffMin}m ago`;\\n  const diffHr = Math.floor(diffMin / 60);\\n  if (diffHr < 24) return `${diffHr}h ago`;\\n  const diffDay = Math.floor(diffHr / 24);\\n  if (diffDay < 30) return `${diffDay}d ago`;\\n  const diffMo = Math.floor(diffDay / 30);\\n  if (diffMo < 12) return `${diffMo}mo ago`;\\n  return `${Math.floor(diffMo / 12)}y ago`;\\n}\\n\\nexport function formatShortDate(isoDate: string): string {\\n  if (!isoDate) return \'\';\\n  const d = new Date(isoDate);\\n  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return \'\';\\n  return d.toLocaleDateString(\'en-US\', {\\n    month: \'short\',\\n    day: \'numeric\',\\n    year: \'numeric\',\\n  });\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Add repository input parsing, curated open-source starter repos, and number/date formatting utilities.\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/format.ts\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\310D\n\305D\001i\024}\023\203\003\220]\v\256p\303DYU\2341\355\214\277\301{\316\235q\252\255\261E\3266\336J>\312\347\377y\240\301\323\234nF\206\201\275\320N\304cR\305\357\321\331{\341\031d\355\312{X\230\236\'\r\267m\203\341r\252\031\243q\236\234B\341\345\231\370\272\275\321\216g\001\253\f\324\254\356\357X\355-\277\337\376\204\343\332g\020\203`\366Q\253I\274j\212\203\277\364\030\271\303x\317\2349\341\nn_\314\214\323\344\343\257Y\207\264\245\355&\371\234\3630\030\371;\312\271\312\177\206\274I4\017\020\254\2331\325\270\212@\275\2718\020(pWx\v\336\216:\364\344]U\253\215/\324\275\020\212k\200*F \006\362\002\251\0266\216\'Y\261\024\242\005\230\324\334^P\270\"\254\031\247\273\307\315\253F\030\002\003[\203\2541\234-X>\tv\247\370\347\346m%\225\004.\313N\023X\305T2>\037\370<;wY\374\366\264\006`4\233\r\205o\251]J*K@\bw\361\372]=4\316\270\270^=\v\315\002\254I\243i\302\206h\224\3013X\256\356\334H\342\365,\032\221\371\254\321\257\342Y\016k1g\217\\)Y9\b;\240\\\2606H&\323\251\211\365\354U\344kU`\214ml\230\217u\020\222\261\237\334\v,T0:!\214owJj@\347T\312\226\216\235\277\243\231-\213\\\236#\363L\227b\376\002\372]/\'P\263\006\256\354:\204`\370\002\332\245\330\253J\223\356\300\000\327K\025\301$c!\226\tLg\vP\212F\300\375Xx\017\242}b\aG\351\035\357:YC\021\203-u4\340/\373\233\a\2129\272N\265\230\b\304`\260\356GJ\004\020\250\033\025\251\023`\335x\206:\242\3154\217\357\341\2350\2433\330\237#\312\253\310\210D\237LS\024\275\261\244nJ\2140%\342n{\325#\226\302NA\215\226C\"\214\340=\216h\372\177J\267\242D\244\275\206\271:z\345\037\244\364\023\356\241\331\264\221\345\250U\203\375\vV\374\334^\3712\017\325\355|y@v9L\236MY\030\377\3774\v\224e1B\277\372@\324\202\0011S\240R\360\f}\331{X\214\337\f\302%\232\220\000\240mb\376|\267\030\236+x\223\321\030\266\246\214\335*\255\271\aSB\301,\307tR\022%\020\035\211\300A\0240\220/\264\237\336y\230M\006m\336\200\\jF\230E\312\233\371*\365\257NT\365g\264ms\006\020N\322h\317e\264\351\206\\\222\362\315P\020\243[\274\371$\267y\032 e\004