  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Diagnosing Default Behavior**\n\nI\'ve got a burning question to solve: Why wasn\'t the AI summarization the default view, as the user expected? My plan involves immediate diagnostics, specifically testing the `/api/ai` endpoint to troubleshoot this discrepancy. I need to understand why the desired AI summaries didn\'t automatically surface for the user.\n\n\n**Analyzing AI Integration**\n\nI\'m now investigating the potential failure of `/api/ai/summarize` or SHA mismatches as the cause of the issue, and I\'m running some tests to verify that. My primary goal is to ensure AI summaries are the default. Conceptually, I\'m exploring an improved presentation\342\200\224grouping recent commits into thematic \"AI Progress Chapters\" like \"Speed & Performance Wins\" or \"Bugs Squashed\". These would feature bullet-point summaries and AI-translated descriptions, always avoiding raw commit messages.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Clarity**\n\nI\'ve decided on the importance of prioritizing the user\'s understanding, so I\'m making the AI Community Story the default view. I\'ll also add a toggle to show the Developer Commit Log, as an option. The previous \"island view\" wasn\'t helpful, so I\'m replacing it with a new Interactive 3D Project Lifecycle Timeline & Flow Visualizer, based in Three.js, which I\'m confident will communicate the project\'s lifecycle more effectively.\n\n\n**Visualizing Project Stages**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the design of the Interactive 3D Project Lifecycle Timeline. I\'m imagining the workflow as four distinct stages, each represented by a dynamic visual element. Stage 1 will feature animated data blocks representing daily commit activity. Stage 2 will display merged pull requests as interlocking teal modules. Stage 3 is a kinetic flywheel showing velocity and contributors. Finally, Stage 4 will be a launch beacon representing the latest release.\n\n\n**Designing Dynamic 3D Stages**\n\nI\'m structuring the 3D timeline into four interactive stages. Stage 1 will show commit activity, Stage 2 merged pull requests, Stage 3 the velocity and contributors as a kinetic flywheel, and Stage 4 a launch beacon for the latest release. The goal is a highly intuitive, visually engaging experience that\'s easy to grasp. Each stage will feature an AI-powered plain-English lifecycle explainer.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "gM8Ca-2pJf-aur8Po5az2Ak"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_14894462571591241161"
      name: "run_command"
      arguments_json: "{\"CommandLine\":\"curl -sS \\\"http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/github/repo?repo=vitejs/vite\\\" > /tmp/snap.json && node -e \\\"const s = JSON.parse(require(\'fs\').readFileSync(\'/tmp/snap.json\',\'utf8\')); fetch(\'http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/ai/summarize\', {method:\'POST\', headers:{\'Content-Type\':\'application/json\'}, body:JSON.stringify({snapshot:s})}).then(async r => console.log(r.status, await r.text()))\\\"\", \"Cwd\":\"/app/applet\", \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\":10000}"
