  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Project Pipeline**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into Batch 2! I\'m deleting the old `FloatingIsland3D.tsx` file. Now, I\'m setting up a new `ProjectLifecycle3D.tsx` component, the interactive 3D Project Lifecycle Pipeline. I\'m starting to design the new project in earnest. It is going to be genuinely useful.\n\n\n**Visualizing Flow Process**\n\nI\'m now focusing on visually representing the open-source software lifecycle. My aim is a design that instantly communicates the process. I\'m imagining a sunlit studio floor with a blueprint grid for context. A luminous glass-and-aluminum track will visually guide animated data-packet capsules through four stages, running from left to right. I\'m starting the design process of Stage 1, the \"Active Coding\" stage, and thinking through how to display commit counts with a live velocity bar.\n\n\n**Designing Stage Composites**\n\nI\'m now refining Stage 2 of the pipeline. I\'ve conceptualized the \"Git Branch Merge Archway\". I envision glowing branch rails merging within a teal-and-chrome gateway arch, visually demonstrating \"Merged Pull Requests\" for all viewers. The next step is starting Stage 3, the \"Community Engine\", and I\'m designing a kinetic velocity gyroscope with contributor pillars to display commit pace and repo contributors. Finally, the \"Shipped Release\" stage will be a milestone progress ring with a release beacon.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Stage Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the stage visuals! I\'m planning floating, interactive stage buttons, each directly tied to 3D geometry. Each button will show the stage\'s key stats: active coding, reviewed & merged, community engine, and latest release, dynamically updated with zero React re-renders. Clicking a stage will smoothly focus the camera and update the AI Story Card for deeper insight, always staying within the Three.js framework.\n\n\n**Implementing AI Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating AI summarization into the Activity Feed. My plan is to make the \"AI Progress Story\" the default view, showcasing Gemini\'s thematic progress chapters as scannable cards. I\'m building storytelling cards with key details like titles, summaries, and impact labels, alongside the plain-English Release Spotlight and a Jargon Decoder. I\'m also implementing an \"Ask AI more about this\" button for deeper insight! I want to ensure a smooth user experience, even during AI processing, with a dedicated shimmer state that\'s far more user-friendly than raw commit logs.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "M9MCa8KNFYq98L0PxPPFqQU"
    tool_calls {
