    response: "I\342\200\231ve redesigned both the progress view and the 3D visualization based on your feedback:\n\n- **AI Story Summary as the Default Progress View**: Instead of listing raw or lightly reworded commit messages, the default progress section now leads with AI-synthesized **Thematic Progress Chapters** (grouped plain-English updates with scannable community wins), translated **Latest Release Highlights**, and a **Jargon Decoder** explaining real technical buzzwords spotted in the repo. While AI summarizes a newly loaded repo, it shows a clean translating skeleton rather than flashing raw git messages; an optional **Per-Change Breakdown** tab remains available for drilling into individual simplified PRs and commits (with original developer commits tucked behind an opt-in toggle).\n- **Interactive 3D Project Lifecycle Pipeline (Replaces the Island)**: Replaced the decorative island with a purposeful, sunlit 4-stage Three.js architectural pipeline showing how open-source work actually flows from left to right:\n  1. **Active Coding** \342\200\224 Live 3D velocity skyline shaped by recent daily commit activity.\n  2. **Reviewed & Merged** \342\200\224 A branch-merge archway gate visually showing how pull requests merge into the main trunk.\n  3. **Community Engine** \342\200\224 A rotating kinetic velocity gyroscope encircled by top-contributor columns.\n  4. **Shipped Release** \342\200\224 A 3D milestone progress ring and launch beacon reflecting progress toward the next release.\n  - Each stage includes live floating 3D-projected metric labels and opens an AI plain-English walkthrough explaining both *what that stage means* and *what\342\200\231s happening in this repo right now*, plus a direct **Ask AI About This Stage** trigger.\n- **Smarter Rate-Limit Caching**: Auto-sync now checks only a single conditional ETag endpoint before refreshing full data, and AI digests are cached per repo commit/release state for faster reloads."
    message_id: "XdYCa-jFDviaur8P5LSSwQM"
